 # 🚀 **Customer Support Email Automation with AI Agents and RAG**
 
+> ## ⚠️ Fork notice: mock-mailbox comparison mode
+>
+> This checkout has been realigned for the JacAgentComparison project. The
+> Gmail polling, RAG retrieval and proofreader loop described below are gone;
+> the LangGraph workflow now implements the same three-stage pipeline as the
+> sibling `CrewAI-LangGraph` and `byLLM` implementations — classify
+> (IMPORTANT / SPAM / NEWSLETTER / PROMOTIONAL / NOTIFICATIONS / SOCIAL /
+> UPDATES) → analyze thread → draft reply — over the shared mock mailbox in
+> `../mock_mailbox/`.
+>
+> Run one batch (needs `OPENAI_API_KEY` in `.env` here or in
+> `../CrewAI-LangGraph/.env`):
+>
+> ```sh
+> .venv/bin/python main.py ../mock_mailbox/datasets/batch_001.json
+> ```
+>
+> Captured drafts land in `mock_output/results_<case_id>.json`, together with
+> the run's LLM token usage and dollar cost (metered by the shared harness);
+> score them with `../eval/score.py`. `deploy_api.py` and `create_index.py` are stale
+> leftovers from the upstream Gmail/RAG version (kept in git history).
+>
+> The original upstream README follows.
+
 ## 📩 **FULL TUTORIAL: Build AI-Powered Email Automation Using AI Agents + RAG!** 👉 [Read Now](https://dev.to/kaymen99/boost-customer-support-ai-agents-langgraph-and-rag-for-email-automation-21hj) 🎯   
 
